 or not reported says which.
 
+### Memory checkup in the desktop app
+
+**Command Center → Maintenance → Memory checkup → Review now** asks your configured model to read those layers and
+propose what to update, merge or remove. It is one model call with no tools, so it cannot write: the result is a list
+of proposals, by layer, each naming its target, its evidence and what must be preserved. Tick the ones you approve and
+**Add selected to chat** puts them in the chat box as a request; Hermes makes them with the normal memory tools once you
+send it, under your `write_approval` setting. A checkup never proposes removing an entry you protected or a fact added
+in the last seven days, and rarely used is not a reason to remove anything: such suggestions are listed under **Needs
+evidence** instead.
+
 ## Duplicate Prevention
 
 The memory system automatically rejects exact duplicate entries. If you try to add content that already exists, it returns success with a "no duplicate added" message.
